Indeed, I think I lean toward chaotic as the
preferable alignment for wizards (though I
don't favor it for many other roles).

Among other things, wizards get the Eye
as their own quest artifact, so wishing for
that is not an option; therefore, there is
no value in being co-aligned with it.  The
Master Key of Thievery is, to me, a more
valuable option than any neutral quest
artifact a wizard could wish for.  (Some
might prefer the Eyes, I suppose, but I
personally don't, unless I need the
slotless MR; wizards generally do not.)

Wizards aren't allowed to be[1] lawful,
and by the time you can wish for an
artifact weapon you probably have
Magicbane already in any case, and as
a Wizard your spellcasting is such that
post-quest with the Eye, and with
hungerless casting, you can use attack
spells preferentially, so given a good
selection of spell books (including at
least one of magic missile hopefully)
it's alright to have a melee weapon
that does only moderate damage.  IMO,
+7 Magicbane is completely adequate
for a wizard (given the above).

If you do choose to wish for a better
weapon, you can get cross-aligned
ones as long as they aren't double-
cross-aligned (by alignment and also
by role, so as to evade your grasp).
For example, you could wish for
Grayswandir regardless of your
alignment, if you are so inclined.
So the need for a decent weapon
is not really a good argument
against being chaotic, for wizards.

All in all, as a _wizard_, I would tend
to prefer being chaotic over neutral,
strategically.

That doesn't hold for most other
roles.

